# Project: UoP / B2B Salary Calculator

## What it is
Vite single-page app. Polish UoP brutto→netto + B2B/ryczałt comparison.
Target: **expats in Polish IT**. Primary user: Serhii, QA Automation Engineer, Wrocław.

## Key files
- `index.html` — entire app (Vanilla JS, no framework, CSS inline)
- `public/job-rules.json` — B2B role list (PKWiU ↔ title, loaded via fetch)
- `vite.config.js` — base is `/UoPB2BCalculator/` in CI; `'./'` locally

## Commands
```
npm run dev          # local dev server
npm run build        # build-job-rules.mjs + Vite → dist/
npm run test:unit    # Vitest — job-rules contract
npm test             # unit + build + Playwright smoke
```

## Key constants (do not change without tax-expert approval)
- ZUS cap: 2024=234 720 | 2025=260 190 | 2026=282 600 zł
- ZUS rates (employee): em 9.76%, re 1.5%, ch 2.45%, health 9%
- KUP annual limit: 120 000 zł | flat fallback: 250 zł/month
- Tax brackets: 12% up to 120 000 zł cumulative income, 32% above
- Kwota wolna: 300 zł/month tax reduction

## Calibration baseline (2025, 27 000 zł brutto)
Jan/Feb exact match: 19 867,99 zł. Annual error target: <1.5%.
Run `npm run test:unit` to validate.

## Languages
All UI text is bilingual EN/PL. Translation object `T` in JS. Always add both languages.
